      "id": "bm25",
      "title": "BM25, intuition first",
      "category": "learning",
      "subcategory": "retrieval",
      "sec": "think",
      "kw": "bm25 retrieval ranking search lexical term frequency inverse document frequency tf idf saturation length normalization rag",
      "retrieval_tags": [
        "bm25",
        "retrieval",
        "search",
        "learning"
      ],
      "text": "Start with the problem: you have a question and a set of notes, and you need to rank which notes are most relevant. Intuition: rare words are stronger clues than common words, and a note that repeats a query word several times is more relevant, but not linearly more relevant. BM25 combines term frequency, inverse document frequency, and document length normalization. A word that appears in every note gets little weight; a rare word gets more. The saturation term stops one repeated word from dominating, and the length term stops long notes from winning just because they contain more words. Limitation: BM25 matches words, not meaning, so synonyms and paraphrases can be missed. That is why this chat uses a small synonym map and why a future version could add embeddings and a reranker. Practice: take three short notes and rank them by hand for the query local RAG privacy.",
